      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1772719245452,
      "text": "Properties",
      "fontSize": 30,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Properties",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "baseline": 27,
      "index": "b0S",
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "autoResize": true
    },
    {
      "id": "m9-yxzjNmzz0iduFuLIgL",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1738.6273046874999,
      "y": 107.5078125,
      "width": 1516.8239453125002,
      "height": 444.81640625000006,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0T",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 801427151,
      "version": 814,
      "versionNonce": 1595880911,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1772719462918,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "These properties must be maintained by you when designing your API.\n\nSAFE - means that no \"side effects\" occur because of this operation. \n    - Don't do \"business stuff\" with a GET or HEAD request.\n\nCACHEABLE - The response message should contain cache-control header.\n    - The response from a post to a location with a 201 status code and a location header\n      may include a cache-control header that some caches will use to make a cache entry for \n      the location.\n\nIDEMPOTENT - Doing this operation multiple times is in essence the same as doing it once.\n    - This means, for example, multiple DELETEs to a resource should always return 204.",
      "fontSize": 29.65442708333331,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "These properties must be maintained by you when designing your API.\n\nSAFE - means that no \"side effects\" occur because of this operation. \n    - Don't do \"business stuff\" with a GET or HEAD request.\n\nCACHEABLE - The response message should contain cache-control header.\n    - The response from a post to a location with a 201 status code and a location header\n      may include a cache-control header that some caches will use to make a cache entry for \n      the location.\n\nIDEMPOTENT - Doing this operation multiple times is in essence the same as doing it once.\n    - This means, for example, multiple DELETEs to a resource should always return 204.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "RAYBfa6YGmrFY_6Gz1iit",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 135.15625,
      "y": 672.125,
      "width": 1485,
      "height": 50,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0U",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1909795393,
      "version": 232,
      "versionNonce": 554169167,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1772719525218,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "The responses suggested here are possible \"defaults\" - more specific variations can be used when the appropriateness of these defaults \nis found to be lacking.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "The responses suggested here are possible \"defaults\" - more specific variations can be used when the appropriateness of these defaults \nis found to be lacking.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "7B_hT9RTw8NikElYDWgcS",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 812.75,
      "y": 919.6666666666667,
      "width": 330,
      "height": 275,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0V",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 648120071,
      "version": 160,
      "versionNonce": 1455249415,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1789581449411,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "GET /shows\nAuthorization: bearer [jwt]\n\n\n\n200 Ok \nContent-Type: application/json\n\n[\n\n]",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "GET /shows\nAuthorization: bearer [jwt]\n\n\n\n200 Ok \nContent-Type: application/json\n\n[\n\n]",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "l_aYRyJjaZFNxWw9w5mvP",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 661.75,
      "y": 1249.6666666666667,
      "width": 1298,
      "height": 150,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0W",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 818055143,
      "version": 517,
      "versionNonce": 1291953031,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1789582375961,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "200 - 299 - These are \"success\" status codes. 200 is \"Ok\", each additional code is Ok, but some nuance.\n300 - 399 - only really use redirects\n400 - 499 - The code making the request screwed up. Not our fault.\n     400 \"Bad Request\"\n401 - Unauthorized - you need to put something in your Authorization header from someone we trust that identifies you.\n500 - 599 - cone of shame for developers / infra folks. The server barfed. Broken code. Bad.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "200 - 299 - These are \"success\" status codes. 200 is \"Ok\", each additional code is Ok, but some nuance.\n300 - 399 - only really use redirects\n400 - 499 - The code making the request screwed up. Not our fault.\n     400 \"Bad Request\"\n401 - Unauthorized - you need to put something in your Authorization header from someone we trust that identifies you.\n500 - 599 - cone of shame for developers / infra folks. The server barfed. Broken code. Bad.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
